import ../../helpers/driver.dl
window input test:
    button "Count"
    code:
        when the "Count" button is clicked:
            set count to this window's state as a pointer to an integer
            store ((the value at count) + 1) at count
set count to 0
set instance to an instance of input test with state (the address of count)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 640 by 480 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set button to the UI layout for element (the control labeled "Count" in (the address of instance)) in (view's layout)
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (button's painted bounds' x + 4.0) (button's painted bounds' y + 4.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (count = 1) reporting "A quick press and release was lost"
queue UI input of kind 3 key 257 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 6 key 257 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (count = 2) reporting "Enter was dispatched more than once"
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's keyboard focus) reporting "Pointer motion stole keyboard focus"
set view's cursor to a UI point at (button's painted bounds' x + 4.0) and (button's painted bounds' y + 4.0)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set view's seconds to view's seconds + 0.016
loop while update UI view (the address of view):
    set view's seconds to view's seconds + 0.016
set paints to view's paint count
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (button's painted bounds' x + 5.0) (button's painted bounds' y + 5.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's paint count = paints) reporting "Motion without a visual change repainted the UI"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Queued inputs are preserved and static motion does not repaint."
